    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.dag_longest_path - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.dag_longest_path.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.dag_longest_path()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Find the longest path in a directed acyclic graph.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.dag_longest_path()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Find the longest path in a directed acyclic graph.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.dag_longest_path()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Find the longest path in a directed acyclic graph.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nFind the longest path in a directed acyclic graph.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L65457-L65555){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.dag_longest_path()\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![DAG longest path](../assets/graphs/dag-longest-path.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"A seven-node DAG whose edges carry task durations. The heaviest chain of tasks, the critical path B, D, F, G, is drawn in the accent color: its durations 3 + 4 + 2 add up to 9.0, more than any other route from a source to G.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nIn a DAG of tasks and dependencies, the longest path is the *critical path*: the chain\nof tasks that determines the earliest possible finish time, so that any delay along it\ndelays the whole project. On an unweighted graph its length is the number of edges; on\na weighted graph (`Graph(weighted=True)`) it is the total edge weight, so weights can\ncarry task durations. Edges without a weight count as `1.0`, and of several parallel\nedges the heaviest counts.\n\nUnlike shortest paths, longest paths are only well defined without cycles, so the graph\nmust be a DAG. The length is available from `dag_longest_path_length()`.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [list[int]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The node IDs along a longest path, in order. When several paths tie, the one ending\n    at (and then extending from) the lowest node ID is returned. An empty graph gives an\n    empty list; a graph without edges gives a single node.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the graph is undirected or contains a cycle.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~dag_longest_path_length`) \n\n:   The length of the longest path.\n\n[](`~topological_generations`) \n\n:   Group the nodes into layers.\n\n[](`~shortest_path`) \n\n:   The shortest path between two nodes.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nWith task durations as weights, the longest path runs through the slow test suite,\nthough the documentation branch starts with the longer first task:\n\n::: {#78f6bce9 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"fetch\", \"compile\", 3.0), (\"compile\", \"test\", 10.0),\n     (\"test\", \"package\", 2.0), (\"fetch\", \"docs\", 4.0),\n     (\"docs\", \"publish\", 1.0)],\n    directed=True,\n)\n[graph.get_label_from_id(n) for n in graph.dag_longest_path()]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n['fetch', 'compile', 'test', 'package']\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### The critical path\n\n`project()` is the plan for opening a made-up café, with an arrow from each task to every\ntask that can't start until it's done, weighted by the days the first task takes. The\nlongest path is the critical path, the chain of tasks that sets how soon the café can\nopen: from signing the lease through the design, permits, build-out, installation and\ntraining. Here each task is sized by the days it takes:\n\n::: {#46374a59 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ncafe = ec.project()\ncritical = cafe.dag_longest_path()\n\n[cafe.get_label_from_id(n) for n in critical]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n['Start',\n 'Sign lease',\n 'Design',\n 'Permits',\n 'Build out',\n 'Install',\n 'Training',\n 'Soft opening',\n 'Finish']\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#feea14ea .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ncafe.plot(\n    layout=\"pos\", highlight=critical, size_by=\"days\", label_by=\"label\",\n    height=360,\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db